3234       *----------------- Data on Physical Fitness -----------------*
3235       | These measurements were made on men involved in a physical |
3236       | fitness course at N.C. State University. |
3237       | Only selected variables of |
3238       | Oxygen (oxygen intake, ml per kg body weight per minute), |
3239       | Runtime (time to run 1.5 miles in minutes), and |
3240       | RunPulse (heart rate while running) are used. |
3241       | Certain values were changed to missing for the analysis. |
3242       *------------------------------------------------------------*;
3243       data Fitness1;
3244       input Oxygen RunTime RunPulse @@;
3245       datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.FITNESS1 has 31 observations and 3 variables.

3262       ;
3263       proc mi data=Fitness1 seed=3237851 noprint out=outmi;
3264       var Oxygen RunTime RunPulse;
3265       run;

WARNING: The default number of imputations has been changed from 5 to 25.
NOTE: The EM algorithm (MLE) converges in 12 iterations.
NOTE: The EM algorithm (posterior mode) converges in 7 iterations.
NOTE: The data set WORK.OUTMI has 775 observations and 4 variables.

3266       proc reg data=outmi outest=outreg covout noprint;
3267       model Oxygen= RunTime RunPulse;
3268       by _Imputation_;
3269       run;

NOTE: Interactivity disabled with BY processing.
NOTE: The data set WORK.OUTREG has 100 observations and 10 variables.

3270       proc print data=outreg(obs=8);
3271       var _Imputation_ _Type_ _Name_
3272       Intercept RunTime RunPulse;
3273       title 'Parameter Estimates from Imputed Data Sets';
3274       run;

NOTE: There were 8 observations read from the data set WORK.OUTREG.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE PRINT printed page 274.

3275       proc mianalyze data=outreg;
3276       modeleffects Intercept RunTime RunPulse;
3277       run;

